# Simulation: Mix two solutions 1:1, then heat from 20°C to 200°C in 10 steps
# The mixed solution has 50 mmol/kg C and 50 mmol/kg Ca
# (each solution contributes 50 mmol/kg, mixed 1:1 means 25 mmol/kg each)
# BUT: if we consider 1 kg of solution 1 + 1 kg of solution 2 = 2 kg total
# Each solution has 50 mmol total, so mixed = 50 mmol in 2 kg = 25 mmol/kg
# 
# Alternative interpretation: the mixture contains 50 mmol/kg of each
# Let's try with the full 50 mmol/kg of each in the mixed solution

SOLUTION 1
    temp      20
    pH        7
    units     mmol/kgw
    C(4)      50
    Ca        50

EQUILIBRIUM_PHASES 1
    Calcite   0   0

REACTION_TEMPERATURE 1
    20   40   60   80   100   120   140   160   180   200

SELECTED_OUTPUT
    -file   mixing_heating3.sel
    -reset  false
    -temperature    true
    -equilibrium_phases  Calcite

END
